    "id": "NAV-CONSUMER-FOREGROUND-01",
    "disposition": "SOURCE_CORRECTED_RUNTIME_NOT_RUN",
    "retained": "All v1 artifacts and its blocked review remain unchanged.",
    "trace": "A successful current load can be accepted while the real mounted surface is inactive. The v1 readiness guard declines and no actual-open attempt is consumed. Original DocumentView activation only emitted diagnostic plus MiniApps consumption; that path did not call mount/load when there were no pending results.",
    "correction": "Exactly232B add a synchronous public didBecomeActive call to the same original readiness guard; exactly43B call it from the original activation notification between unchanged diagnostic and MiniApps statements.",
    "noReset": "No mount/epoch/read/attempt reset, content reload, automatic resend or altered MiniApps consumption."
  },
  "semanticReview": [
    {
      "area": "Authoritative capture",
      "finding": "Expected network comes from the original owned boot before suspension. The binding is acquired once under the original session lease, and all HTTP/contract/identity/cancellation failures propagate into the existing catch/drain path. Optional defaults apply only to explicit injected consumers."
    },
    {
      "area": "Single workspace dependency",
      "finding": "One store is captured by the original workspace owner, passed through Root and Library to cached document models. Account/Space comparisons use exact byte identity. No C imported context is fabricated."
    },
    {
      "area": "Explicit Home state",
      "finding": "Read then requireHomeDestination validate the original current snapshot and destination. Absent, explicit empty, object, builtin and unsupported states remain distinct. Only explicit user actions set or unset; no recovery-route overwrite or guessed builtin destination."
    },
    {
      "area": "Read authority",
      "finding": "Home controls are outside content-edit permission checks; the existing Host APIs retain current READ, original account/run/network and lease validation. canWrite and original mutation permissions are unchanged."
    },
    {
      "area": "Synchronous ACK retention",
      "finding": "Exact prepared intent is saved before commit; immutable operation/workspace/generation/binding/kind metadata is checked in a synchronous lock-protected holder. ACK is retained before the callback returns, independent of later actor-delivery cancellation. No automatic resend or durable-journal claim;256-entry bounds remain."
    },
    {
      "area": "Real document open",
      "finding": "The operation requires a current successful read and actual foreground-mounted surface. A separate mount identity prevents refresh/child-sheet dismissal from rearming it. Date is captured for the actual observed open, not imported timestamps."
    },
    {
      "area": "Cached reopen ordering",
      "finding": "The successor task owns its new identity before it waits for the cancelled predecessor. Old completion checks its own identity before clearing task state; old epoch/mount guard rejects private result delivery. Existing session/lifetime drains retain and join these tasks."
    },
    {
      "area": "Editor preservation",
      "finding": "All six full originals are restored by28 finite inverse rules. Existing draft/composition/save/Undo/related-document/property/drag/Bookmarks/recovery statements and original identifiers are retained outside the explicit additive ownership and lifecycle wiring."
    },
    {
      "area": "Foreground successor",
      "finding": "The explicit current activation callback revisits the same readiness guard only. Repeated activation cannot repeat an already attempted open and inactive/old owners remain rejected."
    },
    {
      "area": "Language",
      "finding": "New labels use the unchanged AnyUIErrorText.text Hebrew/English mechanism. Source reuse does not qualify actual Foundation/SwiftUI/bundle agreement or either opposite App/OS language combination."
    }
